      "explanation": "<p>When n = 1, 5, 9, 13 then <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.781ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"4ex\" height=\"2.746ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -868.9 1767.9 1213.9\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mfrac\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(220,398) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D45B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(600,0)\"><use data-c=\"2B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1378,0)\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(707.2,-345) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g><rect width=\"1527.9\" height=\"60\" x=\"120\" y=\"220\"></rect></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> will give all odd numbers.</p>\n<p>When n = 3, 7, 11, 15 .....</p>\n<p>n <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.505ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -583 778 665\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> 1 will be even but not divisible by 4</p>\n<p>When n = 2, 4, 6, 8 .....</p>\n<p>Then 2n will give all multiples of 4</p>\n<p>So range will be N.</p>\n<p>And no two values of n give same y, so function is one-one and onto.</p>"
